# Tamia4Life — Cursor rules

Load and obey the repo constitution: **CLAUDE.md** (v1 · 24 Aug 2026).

That file is binding. In particular:

- Name the Italian legal frame before specifying a feature. No frame = not ready to build.
- Three hard-separated lanes (A clinico / B mediazione / C formazione). One occupancy at a time.
- Distress routes to Lane A. Triage outcomes are immutable and versioned.
- Do not build wellbeing scores outside A, AI emotional support, symptom-based B/C matching, or B/C individual emotional case-holding.
- Phase 1 gate is **NOT MET**. Say so before Phase 2+ work.
- Do not resolve the seven human-only decisions in CLAUDE.md §11.
- Copy and CMS content must pass the banned-words lint (`scripts/lint-banned-words.py`).
- Every AZM bridge PR ends with `## R&D FEEDBACK — for Claude` (see AGENTS.md).

If this file and CLAUDE.md ever diverge, CLAUDE.md wins.
